  "title": "osf review: lens-driven multi-agent PR review",
  "summary": "Adds a whole review subsystem to osf: a shipped catalogue of 20 review lenses, a roster of coding agents (dsh, omp, opencode, codex, claude) that answer each selected lens, quote verification against the real files, a quorum-based reducer that turns answers into a verdict, and a GitHub Actions workflow that builds osf from the base branch, runs each reviewer in its own job with only its own provider key, and posts the decision. Alongside it, suppression markers gain rule ownership, `osf scan` gains `--no-suppress`, and the changeset risk report gains content-derived trigger signals that select lenses.",
